  {
   "tipo": "explicacion",
   "titulo": "Say hello",
   "texto": [
    "**Ciao** is informal and serves to greet and say goodbye.",
    "With more distance: **buongiorno** is used during the day and **buonasera** from evening or evening; the time of change varies according to location and situation.",
    "To say goodbye: **arrivederci**. Before sleep: **buonanotte**."
   ]
  },
  {
   "tipo": "explicacion",
   "titulo": "You and you.",
   "texto": [
    "**Tu** is «You». **Lei** is used to treat you, the same verbal form as «her.»: **Lei si chiama**. Writing **Lei** with capital is an optional courtesy convention; it is also found in **lei**.",
    "To say your name: **Mi chiamo Anna** (my name is Anna) or **Sono Anna** (I am Anna).",
    "To ask: **Come ti chiami?** (you) or **Come si chiama?** (you).",
    "When you meet someone: **Piacere** (enchanted)."
   ]
  },
